WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.660
Eduardo knows all too well that being kidnapped
and then simply disappearing is the biggest

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.811
danger facing the migrants.

00:00:05.811 --> 00:00:12.630
A few years ago his brother disappeared without
trace as he made his second attempt to reach

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.990
the US.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.460
We got as far as Chiapas.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:23.150
But the police caught me and deported me back
to Honduras.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.890
I went back again to look for him but there
was nothing.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.530
Around 90 members of the caravan currently
making its way north are said to have disappeared

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.590
after getting on two trucks.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.539
The reports from various organisations have
not yet been confirmed.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:46.559
There are differing accounts of the numbers
missing.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:52.319
Some sources say 80, others 100.

00:00:52.319 --> 00:01:00.750
Human rights authorities are looking into
this case.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:05.820
It's feared they may have been kidnapped - and
handed over to organized crime groups active

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.780
in the area where they went missing.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.969
Now, others in the caravan are spooked.

00:01:13.969 --> 00:01:18.920
When Jolvin lost sight of his two friends,
he thought he'd never see them again.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:26.470
"I was really worried that they had disappeared
and I would never hear from them again.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:30.100
We got separated while I was trying to find
space on one of the vehicles.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.350
I had no idea where they had gone."

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.030
Aid agencies say between ten and twenty thousand
migrants have disappeared in the last ten

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.280
years.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.719
That's one reason why people are queuing to
get into this tent.

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:49.409
Inside, they can call their families for free,
to reassure them they are still ok.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.210
"We're gambling with our lives.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:56.859
If you don't fall off the train, you get run
over by a truck.

00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:05.509
MAN
"The Zetas cartel runs everything here.

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:10.080
We're most afraid for the children."

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.220
Because of the danger, the people in the stadium
divide and register according to the region

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.470
they come from.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.040
That way, they hope, any disappearances will
be noticed.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.800
"It's very dangerous travelling between Mexico
City and the US border.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.440
We need to be well organised and able to look
after each other.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.390
We have to know about each other, every individual,
every child."

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:40.670
Organised crime is lying in wait everywhere
on the journey ahead.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.900
The migrants are at risk of kidnapping and
blackmail.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:51.830
"Criminals lure the migrants with fake offers
of work.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:03:03.980
Then they are forcibly held and subjected
to human trafficking."

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:09.140
Attempts to dupe the migrants even take place
within temporary accommodation in Mexico City.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.730
The president of the Mexican federal human
rights commission says migrants are often

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:19.760
approached by people claiming to be officials.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.900
"No-one had heard of this supposed organisation.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:31.080
They offered to take people in lorries in
groups of 18 north and over the border into

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.200
the US."

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.830
The biggest concern for the people in the
caravan is to avoid falling victim to criminals

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.510
exploiting their desperation.

